  "scenes": [
    {
      "narration": "A tariff is sold to you as a tax on foreign countries. In reality, the foreign country pays almost none of it.",
      "shots": [
        {
          "block": "hook",
          "art": "priceTag",
          "props": [
            "x",
            "bill"
          ],
          "lines": [
            "Who really",
            "pays tariffs?"
          ]
        }
      ],
      "id": "s1"
    },
    {
      "narration": "The exporting country writes a cheque of basically zero. The tariff is collected at your border, from the importer.",
      "shots": [
        {
          "block": "stat",
          "art": "home",
          "big": "~$0",
          "label": "paid by the exporting country",
          "props": [
            "x",
            "globe"
          ]
        }
      ],
      "id": "s2"
    },
    {
      "narration": "By definition, a tariff is a tax paid by the importer, not the exporter.",
      "shots": [
        {
          "block": "evidence",
          "sourceId": "wiki-tariff",
          "kicker": "Wikipedia · tariff"
        }
      ],
      "id": "s3"
    },
    {
      "narration": "And the importer passes that cost straight down the line, onto the price you pay at the till.",
      "shots": [
        {
          "block": "truth",
          "art": "priceTag",
          "kicker": "the truth",
          "line": "A tax on you",
          "sub": "dressed up as a tax on them"
        }
      ],
      "id": "s4"
    },
    {
      "narration": "You can watch it land in the consumer price index, the prices households actually pay.",
      "shots": [
        {
          "block": "evidence",
          "sourceId": "wiki-cpi",
          "kicker": "Wikipedia · consumer price index"
        }
      ],
      "id": "s5"
    },
    {
      "narration": "After recent washing-machine tariffs, the price of domestic washers jumped about twelve percent.",
      "shots": [
        {
          "block": "stat",
          "art": "priceTag",
          "big": "+12%",
          "label": "on domestic washers, after the tariff",
          "props": [
            "chartUp",
            "fire"
          ]
        }
      ],
      "id": "s6"
    },
    {
      "narration": "And trade wars invite retaliation, which is why farmers needed tens of billions in bailouts.",
      "shots": [
        {
          "block": "evidence",
          "sourceId": "wiki-tradewar",
          "kicker": "Wikipedia · trade war"
        }
      ],
      "id": "s7"
    },
    {
      "narration": "It is simply a tax on your own shopping cart, quietly collected at the border.",
      "shots": [
        {
          "block": "flash",
          "bg": "red",
          "line": "A tax on your cart",
          "props": [
            "bill",
            "x"
          ]
        }
      ],
      "id": "s8"
    },
    {
      "narration": "So before today, who did you actually think was paying the tariff?",
      "shots": [
        {
          "block": "question",
          "art": "priceTag",
          "line": "Who did you think paid?",
          "sub": "Comment honestly"
        }
      ],
      "id": "s9"
    }
  ]
}